# The creation and annihilation operators of quantum field theory, modeled by the kernel. A quantum field is a collection
# of modes, each holding an occupation number (how many quanta are in it). The CREATION operator raises the count by one,
# the ANNIHILATION operator lowers it, and the NUMBER operator reads it. The vacuum is the empty mode, and annihilating it
# yields nothing (you cannot remove a quantum that is not there). The kernel proves that annihilation undoes creation (a
# quantum added and then removed leaves the mode unchanged), that the vacuum is annihilated to itself, and the asymmetry
# at the vacuum that is the root of the canonical commutation relation: creating-then-annihilating returns the start, but
# at the vacuum annihilating-then-creating does NOT, the +1 of [a, a-dagger] = 1. This is second quantization, how a field
# becomes particles, the same create and annihilate moves the substrate's collision performs on the mesh.

# A mode's occupation number: how many quanta it holds.
form mode
  case empty
  case more
    link prior, like mode

# CREATION: add one quantum to the mode.
task create
  take n, like mode
  like mode
  send back
    make more
      bind prior
        read n

# ANNIHILATION: remove one quantum. The vacuum (empty) annihilates to itself, since there is nothing to remove.
task annihilate
  take n, like mode
  like mode
  fork case, read n
    case empty
      send back
        make empty
    case more
      link prior
      send back
        read prior

# ANNIHILATION UNDOES CREATION: annihilate (create n) = n, for every occupation. A quantum added and immediately removed
# leaves the mode exactly as it was. This is a a-dagger acting as the identity on any state.
rule annihilate-undoes-create
  seat n, like mode
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call annihilate
        call create
          read n
      read n
  calm hold

# THE VACUUM IS ANNIHILATED TO ITSELF: annihilate empty = empty. There is no quantum to remove from the empty mode.
rule vacuum-annihilates-to-itself
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call annihilate
        make empty
      make empty
  calm hold

# THE COMMUTATOR AT THE VACUUM: creating-then-annihilating always returns the start, but at the vacuum annihilating-then-
# creating does NOT. annihilate (create empty) = empty, while create (annihilate empty) = one quantum, not empty. The two
# orders disagree by exactly one quantum at the vacuum, which is the +1 of the canonical commutation relation [a, a-dagger]
# = 1, the source of zero-point energy. Shown here as the order-dependence: create (annihilate empty) is NOT empty.
rule commutator-asymmetry-at-vacuum
  show miss
    call is-equal
      call create
        call annihilate
          make empty
      make empty
  calm miss

# The NUMBER operator reads the occupation, and creation raises it by one: the number after creation is one more than
# before. number (create n) = succ of number n, here the occupation IS the number, so creating adds one quantum.
rule creation-raises-the-number
  seat n, like mode
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call create
        read n
      make more
        bind prior
          read n
  calm hold
